# =============================================================================
# Trivy IaC misconfig baseline — by-design findings (Sec · IaC Scan, INF.22)
# =============================================================================
# Each ID was reviewed individually (NOT a blanket ignore). Real fixes were made
# in terraform for the findings that were genuine gaps — AVD-GCP-0030
# (block-project-ssh-keys) + AVD-GCP-0020/0014 (db log_lock_waits/log_temp_files).
# Below are ONLY the true by-design findings, each with its rationale.
# Re-review whenever the architecture changes. Format: one AVD-ID per line.

# AVD-GCP-0074 — deny_all_ingress (vpc.tf) uses protocol="all". This is the
# explicit DEFAULT-DENY rule (priority 65534); Trivy flags "large port range"
# without distinguishing deny from allow. All-protocols on a DENY is correct.
AVD-GCP-0074

# AVD-GCP-0017 — Cloud SQL ipv4_enabled=true. Akash containers live outside the
# VPC (no peering possible) and can only reach the PUBLIC IP; private-only would
# crash-loop every Akash service in the pg_isready gate. Exposure is mitigated:
# authorized_networks is EMPTY (IAM-proxy connections only) + ssl_mode is
# ENCRYPTED_ONLY (database.tf:14-26). Kamal/GCP fallback uses the private VPC IP.
AVD-GCP-0017

# AVD-GCP-0031 — Ingress Anchor public IP. Architecturally required: CoAP uplink
# from field nodes (Soldier/Queen) + HTTP-ingress termination. Without a public
# IP the Anchor cannot perform its one function.
AVD-GCP-0031

# AVD-GCP-0033 — VM boot disk without CSEK. Google-managed at-rest encryption is
# active by default; Customer-Supplied Encryption Keys add key-rotation infra a
# solo founder on TRL-3 deliberately does not carry (enterprise over-kill).
AVD-GCP-0033

# AVD-DS-0026 — Dockerfile has no HEALTHCHECK. Liveness/readiness is done OUTSIDE
# the container by Kamal proxy (/up->/ready, INF.10) + Akash readiness; a Docker-
# native HEALTHCHECK would duplicate that and needs curl in the slim image.
AVD-DS-0026
